te_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0023123840538405703,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":13.7,"_gate_share_shrink":0.2036727375584646,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":100.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.3139,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Navios Maritime Partners L.P. owns and operates dry cargo and tanker vessels in Asia, Europe, North America, and Australia. The company offers seaborne transportation services for a range of liquid and dry cargo commodities, such as crude oil, refined petroleum, chemicals, iron ore, coal, grain, fertilizer, and containers. It charters its vessels under short, medium, and longer-term time charters. As of March 5, 2026, the company's fleet consisted of 66 dry bulk vessels, 51 containerships, and 53 tanker vessels. Navios Maritime Partners L.P. was founded in 2007 and is based in Piraeus, Greece.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Angeliki  N. Frangou | Chairwoman & CEO | Age 60 | Compensation: $150,000 (FY2025)","financial_summary":["Navios Maritime Partners LP is a mid-cap industrials business with a $2.6B market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +20% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","The business throws off $281M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.77\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn.","Shareholder yield is only 0.2%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 31% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 66% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 65% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Large open-market insider purchases (net $849.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why (NMM) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/34/Why_NMM_Price_Action_Is_Critical_for_Tactical_Trading_111226052802_1794522482.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794522482.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Navios Maritime Partners (NMM) Undervalued As Strong Earnings Raise The Stakes?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https:/